{"id": "q0103", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 867536581, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0c0eb5f5089b4570f4b5f593318ef7c0c5f8ba06a58bdaf93a6686b9afa1d86e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "The data in the table below shows the percent of bus riders in a survey of Central H.S. students; 300 males and 300 females in each grade were surveyed. For which grade is the number of its male bus riders closest to $135\\%$ of the number of its female bus riders? \\begin{tabular}{|l|c|c|}\\hline\nGrade & Males & Females \\\\ \\hline\n$9^{\\mathrm{th}}$ grade & $41.1\\%$ & $39.4\\%$ \\\\ \\hline\n$10^{\\mathrm{th}}$ grade & $34.4\\%$ & $33.1\\%$ \\\\ \\hline\n$11^{\\mathrm{th}}$ grade & $20.6\\%$ & $13.8\\%$ \\\\ \\hline\n$12^{\\mathrm{th}}$ grade & $11.6\\%$ & $8.6\\%$ \\\\ \\hline\n\\end{tabular}\n\nSolve and give the final answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0103.wav", "input_sha256": "adbc6ffc5dc5203fb5bd83ab83bfe8ae216fcd2142658aed2c0feeef3dc61470", "input_samples": 675000, "input_s": 42.188, "n_real_chunks": 43, "score": 0.8105, "act": 0.9998, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Please provide the table of percentages. To solve it once you share the table: for each grade, compare \\[ 300(\\text{male bus rider %}) \\quad \\text{to} \\quad 1.35 \\times 300(\\text{female bus rider %}) \\] Since both groups have 300 students, this simplifies to comparing: \\[ \\text{male %} \\quad \\text{to} \\quad 1.35 \\times \\text{female %} \\] The grade with the smallest difference is the answer.", "expert_answer": "Please provide the table of percentages.  \n\nTo solve it once you share the table: for each grade, compare\n\n\\[\n300(\\text{male bus rider %}) \\quad \\text{to} \\quad 1.35 \\times 300(\\text{female bus rider %})\n\\]\n\nSince both groups have 300 students, this simplifies to comparing:\n\n\\[\n\\text{male %} \\quad \\text{to} \\quad 1.35 \\times \\text{female %}\n\\]\n\nThe grade with the smallest difference is the answer.", "transcript": "The data in the table below shows the percent of bus riders in a survey of Central HS students. 300 males and 300 females in each grade were surveyed. For which grade is the number of its male bus riders closest to 135% of the number of its female bus riders?\n", "asr_s": 3.39, "expert_s": 3.87, "expert_input_samples": 288000, "expert_input_s": 18.0, "expert_input_sha256": "8d6099232c7ec7b296db9a03d4cfb8c8b5f9faf693c8e530479c2b08a945a3f2", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 4.199, "relay_synth_ms": 20495, "onset_chunk": 17, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 2062, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 2062, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0103_balanced_relay.wav", "sha256": "da668191463f2010096e27fd0ca3c137d95964061248588cb461717e3472a0d1", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 46.92}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0103_balanced_candidate.wav", "sha256": "7c63582a210f1d31a865332b633ec0fa26b52e052538dbd920bc9157716db04c", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0103_balanced_stall.wav", "sha256": "5da0ad8e92851238eec9411fcb302d6e9f6c85a106cbeec836c14bfe04785afe", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.92}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.055, 1.099, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.057, 2.104, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.06, 3.106, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.061, 4.11, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.06, 5.108, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.061, 6.109, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.061, 7.109, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.062, 8.111, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.06, 9.108, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.063, 10.112, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.062, 11.11, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.062, 12.111, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.063, 13.111, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.063, 14.1