{"id": "q0125", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3907012978, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "0c0eb5f5089b4570f4b5f593318ef7c0c5f8ba06a58bdaf93a6686b9afa1d86e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 5, "query": "The equation\n\\[x^{10}+(13x-1)^{10}=0\\,\\]has 10 complex roots $r_1,$ $\\overline{r}_1,$ $r_2,$ $\\overline{r}_2,$ $r_3,$ $\\overline{r}_3,$ $r_4,$ $\\overline{r}_4,$ $r_5,$ $\\overline{r}_5,$ where the bar denotes complex conjugation. Find the value of\n\\[\\frac 1{r_1\\overline{r}_1}+\\frac 1{r_2\\overline{r}_2}+\\frac 1{r_3\\overline{r}_3}+\\frac 1{r_4\\overline{r}_4}+\\frac 1{r_5\\overline{r}_5}.\\]\n\nSolve and give the final answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0125.wav", "input_sha256": "1f52f81768ca778d1c9c32eca86e9b0e0335d7d7143914cec4d9a3689828ce13", "input_samples": 499200, "input_s": 31.2, "n_real_chunks": 32, "score": 0.967, "act": 0.9965, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Assuming the equation is \\[ x^{10}+\\frac{13}{10}x^5+1=0, \\] let \\(y=x^5\\). Then \\[ y^2+\\frac{13}{10}y+1=0. \\] The product of the two \\(y\\)-roots is \\(1\\), and since they are complex conjugates, each has modulus \\(1\\). Thus for every root \\(r\\), \\[ |r|^5=1 \\implies |r|=1, \\] so \\[ rk\\overline{rk}=|rk|^2=1. \\] Therefore, \\[ \\sum{k=1}^5 \\frac{1}{rk\\overline{rk}} =1+1+1+1+1=5. \\] \\[ \\boxed{5} \\]", "expert_answer": "Assuming the equation is\n\n\\[\nx^{10}+\\frac{13}{10}x^5+1=0,\n\\]\n\nlet \\(y=x^5\\). Then\n\n\\[\ny^2+\\frac{13}{10}y+1=0.\n\\]\n\nThe product of the two \\(y\\)-roots is \\(1\\), and since they are complex conjugates, each has modulus \\(1\\). Thus for every root \\(r\\),\n\n\\[\n|r|^5=1 \\implies |r|=1,\n\\]\n\nso\n\n\\[\nr_k\\overline{r_k}=|r_k|^2=1.\n\\]\n\nTherefore,\n\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^5 \\frac{1}{r_k\\overline{r_k}}\n=1+1+1+1+1=5.\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{5}\n\\]", "transcript": "The equation x ten plus thirteen i quotient ten equals zero has ten complex roots r one overline one r two, overline r two r three, overline r three r four, overline r four r five, overline r five, where the bar denotes complex conjugation. Find the value of frac one one overline r one plus frac one", "asr_s": 1.58, "expert_s": 16.37, "expert_input_samples": 464000, "expert_input_s": 29.0, "expert_input_sha256": "d3d094e413f521f9f6134dc2321474793f397f52edd63013eb44b09686b85c9a", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 16.777, "relay_synth_ms": 113941, "onset_chunk": 28, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 154, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 154, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0125_balanced_relay.wav", "sha256": "bb8c3313508091badd0267ef493ee69e9ea512261c6f02929b3c75f6a9bb9dda", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 276.28}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0125_balanced_candidate.wav", "sha256": "1b56df541ea7af12dbef9a2a62f470555f9ff8f3346382f6130602192650106f", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0125_balanced_stall.wav", "sha256": "bf703fd4873a6dc6a80a16fe834c37b088acebb688b6a1f3737ed5467aa1c430", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 2.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.057, 1.103, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.057, 2.101, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.061, 3.109, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.06, 4.107, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5.0, 5.06, 5.109, 1, 0, 0], [5, 1, 6.0, 6.06, 6.107, 1, 0, 0], [6, 1, 7.0, 7.06, 7.109, 1, 0, 0], [7, 1, 8.0, 8.06, 8.108, 1, 0, 0], [8, 1, 9.0, 9.062, 9.112, 1, 0, 0], [9, 1, 10.0, 10.059, 10.106, 1, 0, 0], [10, 1, 11.0, 11.062, 11.11, 1, 0, 0], [11, 1, 12.0, 12.061, 12.108, 1, 0, 0], [12, 1, 13.0, 13.063, 13.112, 1, 0, 0], [13, 1, 14.0, 14.063, 14.111, 1, 0, 0], [14, 1, 15.0, 15.063, 15.112, 1, 0, 0], [15, 1, 16.0, 16.06, 16.107, 1, 0, 0], [16, 1, 17